  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_akkord",
      "name": {
        "en": "Akkord's Badge",
        "zh": "协律证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_akkord",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Akkord has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for inflicting exceptionally long-range Arts casualties with a directional aspect.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Caster Operator during field operations to exercise Blast Caster responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员协律擅长在单方向造成超远距法术伤害\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为术师干员，行使轰击术师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_akkord",
      "name": {
        "en": "The Music Box of A Burdenbeast",
        "zh": "移动八音盒",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_akkord",
      "description": {
        "en": "The fields of northern Leithanien are shrouded in a thin blue mist come evening time. The wind blows gently, sending the white flowers scattered across the meadows tumbling as they please.\nTonia has come to gather flowers in place of the town pharmacist, imbuing their petals with pleasant music. They were exceedingly simple Arts, requiring only the marking of miniature symbols into the petals' vasculature. As they sway in the wind, the flowers will play a lingering melody. She crouches down, placing the imbued flowers into her basket one after the other.\nAn aged burdenbeast strolls by the pasture fence, approaching the basket for a sniff before immediately munching on one of the imbued flowers. There is no time for Tonia to stop it. All she can do is listen to the notes spilling out of its throat. After a few steps forward, it too seems to realize that the sound is emanating from its own body. It stops and swivels its ears, constantly letting out brays of its own as it tries to respond to this miraculous melody. The notes warble as the tune is pushed out of its mouth by its breathing, thrumming to the beat of its slow steps under the darkening sky.\nIt is not long before the stockbeasts in the pasture lift their heads in agitation. They soon calm down, gathering by the one musical burdenbeast, but rather than seeming like they are following a leader, it is more like they have recognized a sensation they have not felt in a very long time: the calm before the snowstorm, the crackling of melting streams, and the touch of a refreshingly warm breeze under the afternoon sun. The ranch owner pushes open the door, intending to disperse the gathering, but upon seeing the odd serenity, he stops. The wind, the stamping of hooves, and the distant cries of fowlbeasts are all mellowed by the gentle melody.\nTonia stands by the field. She had meant to return to the pharmacist already, to hand in the flowers and complete her task. But now, she watches the aged burdenbeast as if it were some clumsy musician, slowly performing in the twilight. There is no grand opera at play here, only scattered, isolated voices that have found each other once more. Here and now, they have become the language of the land thanks to this chance reunion.\nThe flowers' melody was only meant to have played for a moment in the wind, but within the burdenbeast's body, the notes seem to have found a new path to follow. As the curtain of night falls, they deepen and soften. Tonia suddenly realizes she has forgotten to record this new melody. But she also feels that, even if the petals have melted away within the burdenbeast, the notes shall not fade. They will remain in the memory of the herd, like a seed hidden within the flowing of the wind, the stillness of the snow, and between the breaths of the fields.",
        "zh": "莱塔尼亚北境的牧场在傍晚时分笼罩上了一层蓝色的薄雾。风细细地吹，吹得散落在草地上的白花随意滚动。\n托妮娅替镇上的药师来采花，然后在花瓣里存储能够安抚情绪的音乐术式。这是一种非常简单的技艺，只需在花瓣脉络上刻下极细的符号，花在风中摇动时便会响起悠长的旋律。她蹲在地上，把刻好了术式的花朵一一放入篮中。\n一头年老的驮兽在牧场围栏边踱步，它凑近篮子嗅了嗅，随即把一朵刻印了术式的白花吞进嘴里。托妮娅来不及伸手去拦，只听见一串音符从驮兽的喉间溢出。往前走了几步后，驮兽似乎也意识到，这些声响出自自己体内。它停下脚步，转动耳朵，随后不住地发出声音，试图去应和那奇妙的旋律。音符随之颤动，那旋律被它的呼吸推着，和它缓慢的脚步一道在暮色下的牧场里移动。\n很快，牧场中的牧兽也抬起了头。那些躁动的动物纷纷安静下来，朝这头驮兽聚拢。但它们的眼神并不像是在追随某个主导者，更像是辨认出了一种久违的气场——风雪来临前的安静，溪水解冻时的叮咚声，午后阳光洒在草场上时，清凉又夹杂着几丝暖意的微风吹拂在自己身上的触感。牧场主推门出来，本想赶开这群聚在一起的动物，却在一片奇异的宁静里停住了脚步。风声、蹄声、远处羽兽的鸣叫声，全都被这低缓的旋律揉得松软起来。\n托妮娅站在牧场边，她原本只想将花瓣带回去交给药师，快点完成这份委托。但现在，她看着那头年老的驮兽像个笨拙的乐手，在暮色中缓慢演奏。没有华丽的起承转合，原本散落的、孤立的声音找到了彼此，在此时此刻，因一次偶然而重逢，变成这一片土地的语言。\n花的旋律本来只能在风中短暂停留，但在驮兽体内，那些音符仿佛找到了新的旅途。等到夜幕降下，旋律变得轻柔，也更加深邃。托妮娅才想起自己忘了要收录这支插曲。但她又觉得，即使花瓣上的纹路在驮兽的体内彻底消散，那些声音也不会消失。它们会留在兽群的记忆里，就像一粒种子，藏在风的流向、雪的静默和草地的呼吸之间。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
